model optimizer: google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it on vllm (GPU), metadata from huggingface
  MoE: 128 experts, 8 per token, 25805936206 params, ~4.0B active -> recorded for the bandwidth model (decode moves the active experts' bytes) [https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it/blob/4d7ae4984b7db7de8f8457170b3f1a419ee76d52/config.json]
  context 262144 tokens -> kept at the agent's own --max-model-len / OVMS default [https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it/blob/4d7ae4984b7db7de8f8457170b3f1a419ee76d52/config.json]
  2 safetensors candidate(s); top: google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it [official] -> serve google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it@4d7ae4984b7d [https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it/tree/4d7ae4984b7db7de8f8457170b3f1a419ee76d52]
  recipe Google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it (vllm@960f5c1bb145) -> tool parser gemma4, reasoning parser gemma4 [recipes/models/Google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it.yaml features.tool_calling, features.reasoning]
  chat template thinks off by default -> thinking off for agents, pinned server-side: --default-chat-template-kwargs '{"enable_thinking": false}' (a request's own kwargs still win; K3D_GPU_AGENT_THINKING=on|off|model) [vllm entrypoints cli_args.py default_chat_template_kwargs (v0.14.0+); https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it/blob/4d7ae4984b7db7de8f8457170b3f1a419ee76d52/chat_template (line 186)]
  generation_config.json: do_sample=True, temperature=1.0, top_k=64, top_p=0.95 -> the engine applies it as the request default [https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it/blob/4d7ae4984b7db7de8f8457170b3f1a419ee76d52/generation_config.json]
  vision tower in config.json; agents send text -> --language-model-only (no encoder memory, larger KV pool) [https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.33.0/vllm/engine/arg_utils.py (L1460, v0.17.0+)]
  drafter google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-assistant [official] -> --speculative-config {"method": "mtp", "model": "google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-assistant", "num_speculative_tokens": 4} [recipe Google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it (vllm@960f5c1bb145) features.spec_decoding.modes.mtp (num_speculative_tokens 4)]
  variant ranking (official > RedHatAI > community/self-built; a lower rank wins only when measured better):
    1. google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it [official]
    2. RedHatAI/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it [RedHatAI]
    excluded: Intel/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-int4-AutoRound (int4, the vLLM target on GPU is bf16)
    excluded: Intel/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-int4-mixed-AutoRound (int4, the vLLM target on GPU is bf16)
    excluded: OpenVINO/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it-int4-ov (openvino-ir, vllm serves safetensors)
    excluded: RedHatAI/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-FP8-dynamic (fp8, the vLLM target on GPU is bf16)
    excluded: RedHatAI/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-NVFP4 (NVFP4/MXFP4: NVIDIA only, no Intel engine documents it)
    excluded: google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-qat-q4_0-gguf (gguf, vllm serves safetensors)
    excluded: google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized (QAT weights serve an int4 target; this target is bf16)
  note: drafter google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized-assistant skipped: QAT drafter, the target is not QAT
  note: MoE target: Google says the 26B A4B drafter may not speed up at batch 1 without good parallelism (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/mtp/overview); if vLLM's V1 runner fails on it, VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1 (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51493); K3D_GPU_AGENT_DRAFT=off turns the drafter off
  engine args: --default-chat-template-kwargs {"enable_thinking": false} --language-model-only --speculative-config {"method": "mtp", "model": "google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-assistant", "num_speculative_tokens": 4}
